  "mechanismSummary": "A 1,4-diketone and a primary amine make a pyrrole. Methylamine adds to one carbonyl group, and two proton transfers through acetic acid give a hemiaminal. Its nitrogen then attacks the second carbonyl group, forming a five-membered ring, and two more proton transfers give 2,5-dihydroxy-1,2,5-trimethylpyrrolidine. Part 2 removes two molecules of water to give the aromatic pyrrole.",
